		{"id":"b3d9c39d35fe5612","type":"group","x":8280,"y":-1104,"width":855,"height":979,"label":"Hair/Fur material"},
		{"id":"3b3870fc7de600be","type":"text","text":"Variable density and light is partially entering surface where it is scattered and absorbed","x":-2563,"y":-2940,"width":250,"height":124},
		{"id":"6cecbee7a99329b8","type":"text","text":"Dielectric objects","x":-2563,"y":-3045,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"f144f3ae43080d4e","type":"text","text":"Storing shading data in object interior gives realistic look.\n\nRepresentation using voxels and global shading is required.","x":-2563,"y":-2780,"width":250,"height":200},
		{"id":"a8ff0c6400145bdb","type":"text","text":"Gas: smoke","x":-2203,"y":-2425,"width":400,"height":80},
		{"id":"c832aa7b845e1edf","type":"text","text":"If voxels contain only bit information (solid opaque objects)","x":501,"y":-3364,"width":359,"height":110},
		{"id":"7a1994a560f5386b","type":"link","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marching_cubes","x":605,"y":-2890,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"0e3d8cfa9348cd5a","type":"text","text":"Converting voxels to set of polygons with culling","x":426,"y":-3020,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"540a9ada4491e794","type":"text","text":"Ray casting to determine nearest hit of each voxel","x":161,"y":-3020,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"7648b7696dcd5fe0","type":"text","text":"Materials in nature and physics","x":-789,"y":-775,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"f8a2dfbc72cadf6a","type":"text","text":"* https://www.ea.com/frostbite/news/physically-based-sky-atmosphere-and-cloud-rendering\n* https://www.sidefx.com/tutorials/creating-stunning-volumetric-clouds-skies/","x":-1760,"y":-1886,"width":745,"height":105},
		{"id":"a32a9591b2fb2a7c","type":"text","text":"If voxels are containing density (translucent/transparent objects)","x":1368,"y":-3364,"width":344,"height":110},
		{"id":"ea52b750789060f7","type":"text","text":"Rendering volume represntation","x":930,"y":-3714,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"cb68eb85d89d7b40","type":"text","text":"Ray-tracing and path tracing","x":1267,"y":-3032,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"947fb1e7bfbe43c0","type":"text","text":"Conversion to level sets for ray tracing","x":930,"y":-3020,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"45d724e90d9241b9","type":"text","text":"Marching cubes for polygonization","x":680,"y":-3020,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"a8011a1311df20ee","type":"link","url":"https://www.scratchapixel.com/lessons/3d-basic-rendering/volume-rendering-for-developers/volume-rendering-summary-equations.html","x":1340,"y":-2870,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"ee91af96374f2915","type":"text","text":"Houdini environment for material modeling:\n* Staging\n* LOPs\n* Karma\n* MaterialX","x":1800,"y":472,"width":307,"height":248},
		{"id":"eca6a398a16bff29","type":"text","text":"Conversion to isosurface and polygonization","x":1540,"y":-3032,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"a63949b08ffaf09e","type":"text","text":"Material modeling is performed in target environment (e.g., Unity, Blender) where final rendering is performed. This is because material I/O is still not standardized and smooth between different DCCs and Game Engines.\n\nTherefore, in this lecture we will use Houdini to create geometry shape and create materials in Blender. Or, we will download model and create procedural material:\n* https://threedscans.com/\n* https://www.myminifactory.com/scantheworld/\n","x":1867,"y":30,"width":804,"height":290},
		{"id":"4a8d18f6a818a9e5","type":"text","text":"Unity environment for material modeling:\n* Shader graph","x":2441,"y":467,"width":250,"height":253},
		{"id":"23a55783754573bc","type":"text","text":"Tool for **rendering**","x":-1637,"y":-3744,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"dd2d084aaa5c53dc","type":"text","text":"* Atmosphere\n* Large scale fog\n* Volumetric lighting\n\n* Sky\n* Clouds\n","x":-1524,"y":-2580,"width":274,"height":220},
		{"id":"9835bc76d2224135","type":"text","text":"Efficient real time global illumination: https://www.icare3d.org/research/GTC2012_Voxelization_public.pdf","x":-879,"y":-2274,"width":940,"height":70},
		{"id":"0697529861834411","type":"file","file":"Images/Material/Tools/SceneVoxelizationRendering1.jpg","x":-339,"y":-2490,"width":400,"height":186},
		{"id":"afc81de4eed1fa28","type":"file","file":"Images/Material/Tools/SceneVoxelizationRendering.jpg","x":-339,"y":-2925,"width":400,"height":399},
		{"id":"15679085b17f90ff","type":"text","text":"Blender environment for material modeling:\n* Shader nodes","x":2149,"y":470,"width":250,"height":250},
		{"id":"8d1e08ddd5c02042","type":"text","text":"Participating media","x":-1512,"y":-2740,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"170568fc46e6d181","type":"file","file":"Images/Material/Tools/SceneVoxelizationRendering2.jpg","x":-879,"y":-2925,"width":459,"height":281},
		{"id":"6bef7e33438387c9","type":"text","text":"Data structure for **light transport**\n* Efficient scene representation for visibility solving and light tracing","x":-519,"y":-3230,"width":360,"height":150},
		{"id":"0e789d2a6c0f06af","type":"file","file":"Images/Material/Tools/SceneVoxelizationRendering3.jpg","x":-879,"y":-2604,"width":459,"height":227},
		{"id":"2cfad1c54f788d04","type":"text","text":"No need to store shading data for object interior.\n\nRepresentation using surface (e.g., polygonal mesh) and local shading suffices.","x":-3561,"y":-2720,"width":249,"height":220},
		{"id":"1638aaae04cdbf61","type":"text","text":"Dense interior where light is almost completely reflected on surface","x":-3561,"y":-2897,"width":250,"height":123},
		{"id":"06ad1850beb9d330","type":"text","text":"Data structure for **shading**:\n* Object interior which affects its look by scattering and absorption\n* Participating media: volume filled with particles which scatter and absorb light\n\nStoring shading parameters: color, density, etc.\n\nUsed for computing **scattering** and **absorption** during shading.","x":-2739,"y":-3450,"width":603,"height":273},
		{"id":"c8e31ff047c5dfa5","type":"text","text":"Metal objects","x":-3562,"y":-3047,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"02f04a4c1b67408d","type":"text","text":"Primjer od Dreamworksa: https://www.openvdb.org/documentation/","x":-4911,"y":-306,"width":451,"height":106,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"335109c1504da30f","type":"file","file":"Images/Material/Examples/VolumeCharactersGas.jpg","x":-4999,"y":352,"width":399,"height":324},
		{"id":"c2f2f140b1761ca7","type":"file","file":"Images/Material/Examples/Cloud.jpg","x":-4999,"y":-62,"width":400,"height":217},
		{"id":"be61cb312d8507b6","type":"text","text":"https://disneyanimation.com/resources/clouds/","x":-4999,"y":155,"width":400,"height":89},
		{"id":"8e41313da6a25be5","type":"file","file":"Images/Material/Tools/Volume_Shading.jpg","x":-2636,"y":-2303,"width":400,"height":190},
		{"id":"4958c4e7e0607c5d","type":"text","text":"Specular","x":-1148,"y":506,"width":250,"height":60},
