		{"id":"fb0ee821203a370a","type":"text","text":"Materials:\n* Dessert, stone, water, ice: https://www.artstation.com/jantru\n* Fabric, stone: https://www.artstation.com/dc-thibaut-r\n* Stone, tiling: https://www.artstation.com/ethanolson\n* Stone, tiling: https://www.artstation.com/victordilman","x":6240,"y":1359,"width":797,"height":203},
		{"id":"0c4acf6096d4e82e","type":"text","text":"Masks for different:\n* Textures\n* BRDFs","x":5735,"y":-871,"width":273,"height":151},
		{"id":"03b91fce5fdb26c0","type":"text","text":"Surface","x":6465,"y":-796,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"412b5353373e5cfd","type":"link","url":"https://docs.blender.org/manual/en/latest/render/shader_nodes/input/particle_info.html","x":5440,"y":640,"width":560,"height":250},
		{"id":"cf949623dd77efb7","type":"file","file":"Images/Material/LectureExamples/2/r1.jpg","x":7293,"y":-937,"width":400,"height":225},
		{"id":"1563e89ed8b8b865","type":"text","text":"**Rendering** e.g., CT scan: color or density stored per voxel is used in shading and light transport","x":-1363,"y":5312,"width":309,"height":118},
		{"id":"a09b2c27527aad9f","type":"text","text":"Example: Smart chunk streaming","x":-1304,"y":5773,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"9f745dbe2644c8af","type":"text","text":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mDQsOpG-Ot8","x":-964,"y":5905,"width":400,"height":50},
		{"id":"3e6d42ed50762406","type":"file","file":"Images/Material/Tools/Maxon.png","x":-684,"y":4196,"width":280,"height":280},
		{"id":"728d503ac69dad10","type":"file","file":"Images/Material/Tools/Voxels.jpg","x":-339,"y":4237,"width":201,"height":198},
		{"id":"71b5d41176603f20","type":"text","text":"Volumes are theoretical representation of:\n* **medium inside object** (its interior inside surface where surface is usually described with polygonal mesh) \n* or **medium between objects** (between surfaces, participating media)\n\nVolumes are in practice represented using **voxels**:\n* Data structure: grid or sparse grid where each cell (voxel) is storing data.\n* Each voxel can contain data such as scalar (scalar field) or vector (vector field).","x":-2340,"y":4336,"width":880,"height":300},
		{"id":"aac2197bf95d59f0","type":"text","text":"Voxel is \"volume element\" (just like pixel is picture element or textel is texture element).\n\nEach voxel represents volume of space, typically a cube in a uniform 3D grid.\n* Index of grid determines the location of voxel.\n* Volume of an object represented with voxels is sum of voxels inside of the object.\n\nVoxels are used to store **volumetric data**. \n* **Scalar Single bit** can be stored per voxel representing whether the center of voxel is inside or outside of an object. This way, solid objects with interior can be represented. \n* **Scalar Float value** representing density, opacity, signed distance or other scalar can be stored per voxel. Voxel grid then represents 3D scalar field.\n* **Vector value** representing volume flow, color, normal, or other vector can be stored per voxel. Voxel grid then represent 3D vector field.","x":-2340,"y":4910,"width":880,"height":460},
		{"id":"b76d7359a63e7489","type":"text","text":"* **Significant memory requirements**: storage requirements grow according to O(n^3) with voxel resolution. Example: resolution of 1000 results in 1000 000 000 locations.\n* **Acceleration structures** and **smart streaming** are required\n\t* **Data streaming** in certain radius around camera (e.g., Minecraft is using 16x16x256 chunks of voxels around player)\n\t* **Coherence** (similar or same values of neighboring voxels) and **sparseness** (lot of voxels are usually empty) allow **compact representations** using **Octree** - only data which differ need to be stored -> **Sparse Voxel Octree** allows LOD (3D equivalent to mipmap)","x":-2325,"y":5686,"width":880,"height":340},
		{"id":"141f093ed326de35","type":"text","text":"OpenVDB\n* Details: https://www.openvdb.org/about/\n* NVIDIA:\n\t  * https://developer.nvidia.com/nanovdb\n\t  * https://developer.nvidia.com/gvdb\n","x":-2325,"y":6073,"width":880,"height":200},
		{"id":"3540049ceec124de","type":"text","text":"Object interior","x":-1374,"y":4299,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"b971bcb70e065c02","type":"text","text":"Participating media","x":-1374,"y":4668,"width":250,"height":60},
